 "gaps_a_reader_can_check_in_this_inventory": [
  "No per-label declared-region overlap exists: `row_fields_available` carries `trusted_over_true` and no `unknown_over_true`, `suspicious_over_true` or `provisional_over_true`, which is why E1.4's own artifact records H-WITHHOLD's first falsifier as not computable from any published column.",
  "The one region-overlap quantity that does exist folds declared regions by maximum, not by union, and four committed entries declare more than one region - `ode/euler_decay_2d` declares twenty-four - so the gap is measured on real corpus shapes rather than hypothetical ones.",
  "E1.4's UNKNOWN ceiling is an absolute area (0.10) chosen against a partition it could not scale: the recomputed increase it breached is 0.288798828125 on every arm that moved the partition, and an arm that never touched the partition (C-withhold) shows the ceiling is silent on relabelling, where the change is 0.0.",
  "The E1.4 freeze states its pilot scope in prose (one entry, two seeds, two budgets) and provides no reduced plan, so the pilot ran the full frozen plan; see the committed `recorded_defects` list in `analysis/e1-4-resolution-demand.json`.",
  "E1.4's corpus had no entry that is both resolvable and over-claiming in coarse leaves: the reference arm's whole certified over-claim is 0.000171 of its domain and 40 of 100 rows over-claim at all, which is why the resolution question was answered by the bar's arithmetic rather than by a case built to discriminate."
 ],
 "per_label_region_overlap": {
  "absent": [
   "unknown_over_true",
   "suspicious_over_true",
   "provisional_over_true"
  ],
  "consequence": "an entry whose regions tile a cell side by side reports the largest tile, so a certified cell covering two declared boxes is scored as covering one of them",
  "geometry_of_the_present_quantity": "the maximum overlap over the declared regions, not the overlap of their union: `Truth::overlap_fraction` folds regions with `best = best.max(...)`",
  "present": [
   "trusted_over_true",
   "trusted_over_true_coarse"
  ]
 },
